\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces The SU Aurigae system. The majority of this photo comprises of wispy arms, which \citealp {Ginski2021} theorise is material from the surrounding medium replenishing the material in the disk. Credit: \citealp {Ginski2021}}}{1}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces Fig. 3 from Drazkowska2023. This figure provides a general scale for the stages of CA.}}{3}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces Fig 1c of \citealp {Pollack1996}. The initial rise corresponds to the runaway planetesimal accretion of phase 1; the long plateau corresponds to the transitionary phase 2; the sharp increasing corresponds to both accretion rates rapidly increasing (and the runaway gas accretion) in phase 3}}{4}{figure.caption.10}%
